Defect: SMI-MISSING-IMPORT https://pysnmp.github.io/pysmi/stable/mib-defects.html#smi-missing-import

The module uses TimeInterval as the SYNTAX of an object without naming
it in IMPORTS. SNMPv2-TC defines the textual convention and the clause
already imports MacAddress, RowStatus and TruthValue from it.

The repair adds TimeInterval to that existing FROM group. Until it was
written down the compiler supplied the same import on every build, which
compiles but leaves the checked-in text saying something it does not
mean.

--- a/CISCO-LWAPP-SYS-MIB
+++ b/CISCO-LWAPP-SYS-MIB
@@ -24,7 +24,7 @@
         FROM SNMPv2-CONF
     MacAddress,
     RowStatus,
-    TruthValue
+    TruthValue, TimeInterval
         FROM SNMPv2-TC
     SnmpAdminString
         FROM SNMP-FRAMEWORK-MIB
